# Machine-local agent config, written by Connect (apps/gui/src/main/providers.ts).
# `.mcp.json` (Claude Code's own project-scope file, written by `claude mcp add
# -s project`), `.codex/config.toml` (codex) and `opencode.json` (opencode) all
# carry the same portable installer-owned launcher since GUI-149 — no absolute
# paths — but they are still a per-machine opt-in ("this user has Kanmer
# installed and Connected this host"), not project source, and Connect writes
# the same rules into every target project's .gitignore (`connectIgnoreEntries`).
# `.grok/config.toml` is legacy grok residue retired on reconnect. Files written
# before GUI-149 hardcode this machine's Kanmer install and board worktree, which
# is one more reason they stay untracked. `.claude/skills/`, `.opencode/skills/`,
# `.grok/skills/` is a legacy local copy of the plugin skills (the canonical
# ones are plugins/kanmer/skills/). Antigravity now owns skills/MCP in its user
# plugin; its old `.agents` paths are migration inputs, not active writers.
# Keep those paths ignored while a reconnect has not yet retired residue from
# an older checkout; they are machine-local state, never source files.
# Note `.agents/plugins/marketplace.json` is NOT here — it's a real repo file,
# not a Connect-written artifact, so `.agents/` itself is never blanket-ignored.
# All of the below are untracked deliberately — and `scripts/release.mjs`
# counts untracked files as a dirty tree, so leaving them here blocks every
# release. Every `copySkills` destination and every `connectIgnoreEntries()`
# path in providers.ts is checked against this file by tests in
# apps/gui/src/main/providers.test.ts.
.mcp.json
.codex/config.toml
.grok/config.toml
opencode.json
.claude/skills/
.opencode/skills/
.grok/skills/
.agents/mcp_config.json
.agents/skills/

# Machine-local operator inputs, never source: the operator's goal brief, the
# Infisical CLI's project pointer, and the local skills lockfile. Like the
# Connect-written paths above they are untracked deliberately, and
# `scripts/release.mjs` counts untracked files as a dirty tree, so leaving them
# unignored blocks every release (SKILL-039).
goal.md
.infisical.json
skills-lock.json
